## Tutorials

CSS Flexbox is short for the CSS Flexible Box Layout module.

Flexbox is a layout model for arranging items (horizontally or 
vertically) within a container, in a flexible and responsive way.

Flexbox makes it easy to design a 
flexible and responsive layout, without usingfloator positioning.

Try it Yourself »

A flexbox always consists of:

The element below represents aflex container(the blue area) with threeflex items.

### Code Examples

```
<html>
<head>
<style>
.container {
display: flex;
background-color: DodgerBlue;
}
.container div {
background-color: #f1f1f1;
margin: 10px;
padding: 20px;
font-size: 30px;
}
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div 
  class="container">
<div>Item 1</div>
<div>Item 2</div>
<div>Item 3</div>
</div>
</body>
</html>
```

